Generated by `ExpectedArticlesModule.text` of
`gezi/proofs/src/test/scala/gezi/proofs/ExpectedArticlesModule.scala` from the expected
articles `gezi/tests/opentheory_article_expected/*.art`, which are the source; not edited.
The articles were converted from the old writer's output to the thunk constants of D7.1
(https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1561); the generator of the articles is the open G3 TODO.
One definition per article: its lines, without their newlines, in order; an article of more than
5000 lines is the concatenation of its parts of 5000 lines, each a definition of its own, since
Lean elaborates a list literal as deep as it is long. The test
`ExpectedArticlesModuleTest.theLeanModuleOfTheExpectedArticlesIsTheirRegeneration` checks that
regenerating this module from the articles gives it byte for byte. The package does not read the
files itself: its Nix build (`gezi/modules/lean.nix`) has only `gezi/lean` as its
source. The module `EndToEndFixtures` takes four articles of the hand-made runs through the
end-to-end theorem; the Lean text of
`LeanStatementsTest.leanAcceptsTheModuleAndMatchesTheArticlesImports`, outside the package, takes
all six articles of the hand-made runs, `two_thunks_of_one_class` and
`an_argument_dropped_then_spelled` among them. The module `FixpointRunFixtures` takes the seven
articles of the fixpoint runs, the runs of the baseline's search strategy of
`FixpointRunModules.runs`.
-/

